<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vittorio Veneto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24 October – 4 November <a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vittorio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veneto">Veneto</a> was the final Italian offensive of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, fought from 24 October to 4 November 1918. Italian forces with British and French support crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piave">Piave</a> and split the Austro-Hungarian army, which disintegrated as the empire itself broke apart. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-villa-giusti">Armistice of Villa Giusti</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> took several hundred thousand prisoners.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vittorio-veneto.jpg" alt="Battle of Vittorio Veneto" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Vittorio_Veneto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
